==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|scilt}}, {{m|goh|scild}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*skelduz||shield}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*(s)keit-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*(s)keid-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kheit-||shield, cover}}. Compare Dutch {{m|nl|schild}}, English {{m|en|shield}}, Danish {{m|da|skjold}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ʃɪlt]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Schild.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}
* {{homophones|schilt|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|g2=n|Schilds|gen2=Schildes|Schilde}}

# [[shield]], [[buckler]]

====Declension====
{{de-decl-noun-m|(e)s|e}}

====Usage notes====
In formal use ([[Standard German]]), the word ''Schild'' in this sense is exclusively masculine. However, in large parts of especially the north and the middle of the German [[Sprachraum|sprachraum]] (language area), the word is mostly or exclusively neuter in speech in all senses of the word, and its plural forms are like those of ''das Schild'', i.e. ''die Schilder'' etc.<ref>[http://www.wienerzeitung.at/meinungen/glossen/389738_Der-Schild-oder-das-Schild.html Der Schild oder das Schild?], Wiener Zeitung Online</ref>

